[ti:Day 06]

[00:00.00]standstill [ˈstændstɪl]n. 停止，停顿 搭 at a standstill 处于停顿状态 / come to a standstill 停顿下来
[00:08.52]subjugate [ˈsʌbdʒuɡeɪt]vt. 使屈从，使服从；征服；克制， 抑制 例 The problem is how to subjugate the rivals at a lower cost.
[00:19.32]packing [ˈpækɪŋ]n. 包装；包装法；包装材料 例 The packing charge of this article is about 5% of its total cost.
[00:29.16]carton [ˈkɑːtn]n. 硬纸盒；纸板箱；一纸板箱(或纸盒)的 量 例 We hope that you will agree to our opinion and accept our carton packaging. 搭 a carton of 一盒
[00:42.36]contaminate [kənˈtæmɪneɪt]v. 弄脏；污染；损害 例 We continually wage war on the insects, for they contaminate our food and carry diseases.
[00:55.68]competition [ˌkɒmpəˈtɪʃn]n. 竞争 例 Thei r goals have been to stimulate competition, promote efficiency and benefit consumers. 搭 in competition with 与…竞争
[01:11.16]monologue [ˈmɒnəlɒɡ]n. (戏剧)独白；滔滔不绝的讲话 例 He went into a monologue on his last day at the company.
[01:20.88]consist [kənˈsɪst]vi. 由…组成，构成；存在于；协调，一 致 例 Most of these groups consist of graduate students and faculty, but some undergraduates join as well. 搭 consist in 存在于 / consist of 由…组成 / consist with 与…一致
[01:40.80]grocery [ˈɡrəʊsəri]n. [ pl.] 杂货；食品杂货店；杂货业 例 He was employed in a local grocery store as a delivery boy.
[01:51.12]priority [praɪˈɒrəti]n. 优先；优先权；优先考虑的事 例 The development of technology is a top priority of the company. 搭 take priority over 比…享有优先权
[02:04.68]eligible [ˈelɪdʒəbl]a. 具备条件的，合格的 n. 合适的人 选；合格者 例 Anyone obtaining an MBA degree is eligible to apply for the position of manager in our company. 搭 be eligible for 合格的；有…资格的
[02:21.96]statute [ˈstætʃuːt]n. 法令，法规；章程，条例 搭 by statute 依据法规
[02:27.36]disorientate [dɪsˈɔːriənteɪt]vt. 使迷失方向 例 I felt completely disorientated by the maze of streets.
[02:37.44]recurrent [rɪˈkʌrənt]a. 复发的；周期性的
[02:41.04]verbalise [ˈvɜːbəlaɪz]vt. 描述；用词语表达 例 He found it really hard to verbalise the concepts of this design.
[02:51.48]buoyant [ˈbɔɪənt]a. (价格等)上涨的，高价的；有浮力的 例 Some businesses have proved they are able to keep sales buoyant even in a tough market. 搭 buoyant cable 漂浮电缆
[03:06.48]perception [pəˈsepʃn]n. 感知(能力)，觉察(力)；观念；看法
[03:11.28]assembly [əˈsembli]n. 装配；集会，集合 例 The company hopes for some cost cuts after the installation of this new automated assembly line.
[03:24.48]elaborate [ɪˈlæbərət]a. 精细的；详尽的；精心计划的 [ɪˈlæbəreɪt]v. 详细说明 例 We're here to elaborate our requirements for the trademark design. 搭 elaborate on 详细说明
[03:39.72]commerce [ˈkɒmɜːs]n. 商业；贸易 例 Gates is not only outstanding in technology. What is more significant is that he gets through the crux passway between technology and commerce.
[03:57.24]hoard [hɔːd]n. 贮藏；聚藏(物) v. 贮藏，囤积 例 The futures market does sometimes signal that prices are likely to rise, which might prompt speculators to hoard oil in anticipation. 搭 hoard up 聚集
[04:15.48]inroad [ˈɪnrəʊd]n. 突然侵袭；损害，侵犯；花费 例 The R&D team has made considerable inroad on this project.
[04:25.08]prestigious [preˈstɪdʒəs]a. 享有声望的；声望很高的
[04:29.52]high-profile [ˌhaɪˈprəʊfaɪl]a. 高姿态的；高调的，备受瞩目 的；知名度高的
[04:35.40]ingredient [ɪnˈɡriːdiənt]n. (混合物的)组成部分；(烹调的)原 料；(构成)要素，因素 例 Passion is a key ingredient in our work and life.
[04:46.80]clue [kluː]n. 线索；暗示 vt. 暗示；为…提供线索 例 In an efficient market, past performance is not only no guarantee of future performance, it offers no clue whatsoever. 搭 clue on 提示 / give a clue to sth. 提供关于 某事的线索
[05:06.48]plethora [ˈpleθərə]n. 过剩；过多；多血症 搭 a plethora of suggestions 意见纷呈
[05:13.20]explore [ɪkˈsplɔː(r)]v. 探测；探索 例 The new market needs to be explored to gain a bigger market share.
[05:23.04]destabilise [ˌdiːˈsteɪbəlaɪz]vt. 使不稳定；破坏…的稳定 例 Any change in the food chain is likely to destabilise the entire ecosystem.
[05:35.76]all-round [ˌɔːlˈraʊnd]a. 多方面的；多才多艺的 例 The enterprise has undertaken all-round technological renovation.
[05:46.92]amass [əˈmæs]vt. 收集；积聚(尤指财富) vi. 集合 例 If you want to amass money, your aim is to extinguish the competition, putting yourself in a position where you can set the price.
[06:03.60]realise [ˈriːəlaɪz]v. 变卖；(把证券等)变现；获(利 搭 realise from/on 从…获利
[06:10.08]forklift [ˈfɔːklɪft]n. 铲车；叉式升降机
[06:13.56]backpedal [ˌbækˈpedl]vi. 变卦；打退堂鼓 例 She later sought to backpedal by insisting that she has been to America before. 搭 backpedal on 就…变卦
[06:27.12]dumping [ˈdʌmpɪŋ]n. 倾销
[06:29.52]fill [fɪl]vt. 装满；填充；担任(职务)；满足(要求等)； 供应(订货) 搭 fill a position of 担任…的职务 / fill backward 返回填补 / fill in for sb. 替代某人
[06:40.92]consistent [kənˈsɪstənt]a. 坚持的，一贯的；一致的，符合 的 例 There is a consistent thread running through all these policies. 搭 be consistent with 与…一致
[06:54.96]circular [ˈsɜːkjələ(r)]a. 圆形的，环形的；循环的；巡回 的 n. 通知，公告；传单 例 Circular references are not always bad and, in fact, are sometimes absolutely necessary.
[07:10.08]nib [nɪb]n. 钢笔尖；尖突，尖端 vt. 给…装上尖头； 削尖
[07:13.80]acceptance [əkˈseptəns]n. 接受；领受；承兑 例 There is often a certain lag between scientific invention and cultural acceptance.
[07:26.28]denomination [dɪˌnɒmɪˈneɪʃn]n. 面额，票面金额 例 The dealings took place on the black market through unofficial gold traders in exchange for high denomination banknotes.
[07:43.08]complement [ˈkɒmplɪmənt]n. 补充；互补的东西；编制名额； 装备定额；补(足)语 [ˈkɒmplɪment]vt. 补充；与…相配 例 I believe you will come to complement them, though you do not want to duplicate efforts. 搭 complement each other 相辅相成
[08:03.48]debenture [dɪˈbentʃə(r)]n. 借方；公司债券
[08:07.32]yeoman [ˈjəʊmən]n. 自耕农；仆人
[08:10.08]vigorous [ˈvɪɡərəs]a. 有力的；强劲的；活跃的
[08:13.80]abolish [əˈbɒlɪʃ]vt. 废除，废止；完全破坏 例 The association wanted to change the constitution to abolish direct elections to the presidency.
[08:27.36]identical [aɪˈdentɪkl]a. 同一的，完全相同的 例 My opinion is not identical to his. 搭 be identical with 与…相同
[08:37.20]underemployed [ˌʌndərɪmˈplɔɪd]a. 未充分就业的；被低聘的；学 非所用的
[08:42.96]yield [jiːld]v. 产出，产生；让渡，让与 n. 产量，产 额；收益 搭 yield to 屈服，让步
[08:48.72]distress [dɪˈstres]n. 亏本出售；被扣押的财物 v. 扣押 a. 亏本出售的；廉价商品的 例 Business competitors always take advantage of each other's distress resulting from the economic downturn to increase their market share.
[09:08.76]backpack [ˈbækpæk]n. 背包，背囊 vt. 背负 vi. 背着背包徒 步旅行 例 The tag on your backpack tells me what it is made of. 搭 backpack transmitter 便携式发射机
[09:21.84]amend [əˈmend]v. 修改，修正；修订；改进，改良 例 Congress may amend the proposed tax bill. 搭 amend one's way 改过自新
[09:31.80]coherence [kəʊˈhɪərəns]n. 一致；连贯性；凝聚；黏合 例 Successful expansions are about coherence as well as price.
[09:42.36]perfumery [pəˈfjuːməri]n. 香水，香料；香料制造法；香料 店
[09:47.04]inventory [ˈɪnvəntri]n. 库存目录；清单；存货；细账 vt. 列 出…的清单；编入目录 例 To establish the product inventory, all the relative data and materials must be classified carefully. 搭 take inventory 清查存货；编制清单
[10:06.24]forthcoming [ˌfɔːθˈkʌmɪŋ]a. 随手可得的；即将到来的；抱合 作态度的 例 Are there any new applications planned for design or development or implementation for the forthcoming year? 搭 forth coming book 近期出版图书 / forthcoming holiday 即将到来的假日
[10:28.56]inconvertible [ˌɪnkənˈvɜːtəbl]a. 不能转换的；不能兑换的 例 Foreign currency is inconvertible in this bank.
[10:38.64]hypothesis [haɪˈpɒθəsɪs]n. 假说，假设；前提 例 What would it mean for the efficient market hypothesis if the market rallied on the news?
[10:51.60]domestic [dəˈmestɪk]a. 国内的；家(庭)的，家用的 例 According to the investigation, low prices have crippled domestic output and foreign imports. 搭 domestic violence 家庭暴力
[11:08.04]municipal [mjuːˈnɪsɪpl]a. 市政的；市立的；地方性的；地方 自治的
[11:13.08]falter [ˈfɔːltə(r)]vi. 蹒跚；衰退；结巴地说话；动摇， 畏缩 n. 颤抖；犹豫 例 Will the economic miracle falter or even collapse?
[11:23.76]quorum [ˈkwɔːrəm]n. 法定人数；选出的一组人 例 The meeting was adjourned because there was insufficient quorum.
[11:34.08]slender [ˈslendə(r)]a. 微薄的；极少的；细长的；苗条的
[11:38.40]mentor [ˈmentɔː(r)]n. 有经验的顾问 vt. 做…的良师；指 导 例 The mentor needs the support of management.
[11:47.40]prepaid [ˌpriːˈpeɪd]a. 预付的
[11:50.28]upscale [ˌʌpˈskeɪl]a. 质优价高的；迎合高层次消费者的； 高档的；有声望的 例 The restaurant is well-known as an upscale restaurant for professionals.
[12:03.24]eccentric [ɪkˈsentrɪk]a. 古怪的，怪癖的 n. 古怪的人 例 The femal manager is regarded as something of an eccentric.
[12:13.68]front-line [ˈfrʌntlaɪn]a. 前线的，第一线的；第一流的 例 The value zone has naturally shifted to the frontier where front-line employees and customers interact.
[12:28.92]ban [bæn]vt. 取缔，禁止 n. 禁令；禁止 例 The trade of seal pelts and meat was curtailed by a 2012 Import Ban. 2012
[12:38.88]outpace [ˌaʊtˈpeɪs]vt. 超过；发展快过…记联想记忆： out(出)+pace(步伐)→超出了别人的步伐→发展快 过…例 The company has outpaced its rivals in the market share. 该公司已经在市场份额上超过 其对手们。
[12:54.60]rental [ˈrentl]n. 租金额，租金收入；租赁 a. 租用的； 收取租金的
[12:59.16]brunch [brʌntʃ]n. 早午餐 vi. 吃早午餐 例 On Sundays, many Americans get up late and go out for brunch.
[13:08.40]shoestring [ˈʃuːstrɪŋ]n. 鞋带；零钱；小额资本 a. 小本经营 的；微薄的
[13:13.68]reciprocal [rɪˈsɪprəkl]a. 互惠的；相互的；对等的 n. 互相起 作用的事物
[13:19.08]makeshift [ˈmeɪkʃɪft]n. 权宜之计；临时措施；临时代用品 a. 权宜的；临时代用的 例 This makeshift kiosk is on the outskirts of the city.
[13:30.24]beneficial [ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl]a. 有益的，有利的；有使用权的；可受 益的 例 He believes that the stability of actual and expected inflation of around 2% has been hugely beneficial to society. 搭 be beneficial to 对…有益
[13:49.32]altruistic [ˌæltruˈɪstɪk]a. 利他的，不自私的；利他主义的 例 The public doubt whether several actors' motives for donating the money are altruistic.
[14:03.24]contrive [kənˈtraɪv]v. 设法做到；谋划，策划 搭 contrive to do sth. 想方设法做成某事
[14:09.96]precise [prɪˈsaɪs]a. 精确的，准确的；恰好的；丝毫不差 的；精密的；严谨的 搭 at the precise moment 正好在那个时刻 / to be precise 确切地讲
[14:20.28]balance [ˈbæləns]n. 收支差额；结余，结欠；平衡 例 The balance in my account is not enough to buy a car.
[14:29.16]holdup [ˈhəʊldʌp]n. 耽搁，停顿；(容器内的)残液；滞留 量；索高价
[14:33.96]scroll [skrəʊl]n. 卷轴，卷形物；名册 v. (使)成卷形 例 Please scroll through the document using the slider bar till you come to page forty. 搭 scroll bar 滚动条
